+| Keep reading | 8/10 | Chapter 7, the assessment notice beginning “Assay-provision enrollee,” followed by the four friends on the wall | The clause and transfer have paid off locally, while the fixed baseline, Lira's bracket, Brom's cohort, and the watchers give the next movement concrete pressure. The ending poses a choice rather than merely announcing danger. | High |
+| Interest / freshness | 8/10 | Chapter 1, Karis explaining why she will try to kill the assay clause; Chapter 6, Cael burning the sixty-three entries | Treating legal research and honest record-keeping as forms of adventure feels specific and fresh. Some younger readers may lose momentum in the repeated repeal-and-consolidation detail before the physical bout arrives. | Medium-high |
